 "note": "X_ITE 16.6.0: one `range`, two levels. Level 1 when the eye-space distance of `center` (through geoSystem and GeoOrigin) is strictly below range, else level 0. Level 0 draws the root (a red 20 m box); level 1 draws the four children together (green, blue, yellow, cyan 10 m boxes at the corners, in the GeoLOD frame) once all four are loaded. The camera is at z 200, the GeoLOD moves with its parent: distance = 200 - T.z (99.9 gives 1, 100.1 gives 0, exactly 100 gives 0). The parent scale counts (the eye-space distance of an offset centre). East is +X with rotateYUp and +Y without; 0.00045 degrees of longitude is 50.094 m. A run-time change of range is followed, 0 and negatives are always level 0. rootNode wins over rootUrl (GL5 draws its blue rootNode, the cyan rootUrl box is never shown). Level 1 with no child content draws nothing (GL6).",
 "gaps": [
